1
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:10,380
Enjoy.

2
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:20,660
Thank you.

3
00:00:21,750 --> 00:00:25,450
Call if you need anything.

4
00:00:31,490 --> 00:00:33,260
Monou?

5
00:00:34,990 --> 00:00:36,590
Sorry.

6
00:00:36,590 --> 00:00:40,360
I don't recall seeing that individual before.

7
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,420
Right. She's a new hire, named Takizawa.

8
00:00:43,420 --> 00:00:47,370
I'm sorry, I should have introduced you.

9
00:00:47,370 --> 00:00:52,180
She's a hard worker,
so please be easy on her.

10
00:00:52,910 --> 00:00:54,390
Of course.

11
00:00:56,620 --> 00:00:58,780
Sui.

12
00:01:00,570 --> 00:01:04,080
I never imagined we'd reunite so quickly.

13
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:06,490
What an absolute surprise.

14
00:01:07,740 --> 00:01:09,860
- Why...
- "Why"?

15
00:01:09,860 --> 00:01:11,920
I work here.

16
00:01:11,920 --> 00:01:14,960
Didn't my Hirose tell you?

17
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:20,910
You'd better not get in my way again.

18
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,270
I'll talk to you soon.

19
00:02:47,020 --> 00:02:48,450
Hello?

20
00:02:48,450 --> 00:02:51,960
This is Takizawa,
from Hirose Architects, speaking.

21
00:02:51,960 --> 00:02:55,030
<i>I forgot to inform you earlier,</i>

22
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:58,480
<i>but I will be your point of contact now.</i>

23
00:02:59,140 --> 00:03:00,300
What?

24
00:03:00,300 --> 00:03:05,530
Please send any details for Hirose my way.

25
00:03:07,530 --> 00:03:10,910
Or did you find issue corresponding with me?

26
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:14,550
No, not at all. I understand.

27
00:03:14,550 --> 00:03:16,410
Thank goodness.

28
00:03:16,410 --> 00:03:19,960
I am excited to coordinate
this project with you.

29
00:03:19,960 --> 00:03:23,470
Have a wonderful day.

30
00:03:28,730 --> 00:03:31,540
This is my proposed schedule for the day-of.

31
00:03:31,540 --> 00:03:33,730
Here are your profiles

32
00:03:35,270 --> 00:03:38,310
for all our guests that day,

33
00:03:38,310 --> 00:03:41,380
as well as an emcee script.

34
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:52,500
Thank you. These are all incredibly detailed.

35
00:03:52,500 --> 00:03:54,590
Thank you, Mr. Hoshina.

36
00:03:54,590 --> 00:03:57,440
Send these over for Hirose
to look over as well.

37
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:59,590
Yes, sir.

38
00:03:59,590 --> 00:04:01,980
I'll ask if there are any edits
to be made as well.

39
00:04:01,980 --> 00:04:03,240
Thanks again.

40
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,760
Of course.

41
00:04:05,830 --> 00:04:08,050
She works quick.

42
00:04:08,050 --> 00:04:10,480
Someone's way too excited about this.

43
00:04:14,240 --> 00:04:17,870
[Proposal - Monou]

44
00:04:17,870 --> 00:04:20,130
[Proposal - Takizawa]

45
00:04:20,130 --> 00:04:21,280
[Your file has been renamed]

46
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:24,960
Thanks for the file.

47
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:27,290
Monou.

48
00:04:27,290 --> 00:04:29,970
Has Hirose gotten back to us
about the event?

49
00:04:29,970 --> 00:04:31,620
Not yet.

50
00:04:31,620 --> 00:04:33,490
I'll reach out about it again.

51
00:04:33,490 --> 00:04:37,310
Too bad. He must be busy.

52
00:04:37,310 --> 00:04:38,270
Let me know how it goes.

53
00:04:38,270 --> 00:04:39,790
Yes, sir.

54
00:04:45,340 --> 00:04:46,780
Everything all right?

55
00:04:46,780 --> 00:04:50,630
Huh? Yeah, it's going fine.

56
00:04:50,630 --> 00:04:52,180
But...

57
00:04:54,150 --> 00:04:58,610
I want to chip away at this alone
for a little longer.

58
00:05:02,980 --> 00:05:04,620
Okay.

59
00:05:16,260 --> 00:05:18,930
[Sui Monou]

60
00:05:19,970 --> 00:05:24,960
Takizawa. Has Idea gotten back to us
about the talk event?

61
00:05:24,960 --> 00:05:27,610
I've tried contacting Monou,

62
00:05:27,610 --> 00:05:30,260
but I haven't been able to reach her.

63
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:32,880
I see.

64
00:05:32,880 --> 00:05:34,930
Thanks again.

65
00:05:34,930 --> 00:05:37,280
Hirose.

66
00:05:37,280 --> 00:05:40,840
I don't know if I should mention this, but...

67
00:05:42,640 --> 00:05:47,320
I used to work at the same company as Monou.

68
00:05:47,320 --> 00:05:49,160
Huh?

69
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:53,950
I'm sorry I didn't bring it up earlier.

70
00:05:53,950 --> 00:05:56,290
But now, I can't help but worry.

71
00:05:56,290 --> 00:05:59,750
Monou tends to keep problems to herself.

72
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:02,740
So, perhaps this delay
is for a similar reason.

73
00:06:05,110 --> 00:06:09,560
Monou does seem to hold herself
quite responsible.

74
00:06:09,560 --> 00:06:12,480
She likely hopes to deliver on her idea.

75
00:06:12,480 --> 00:06:14,970
Even so, we are running short on time.

76
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:17,570
I know this may seem a bit forward,

77
00:06:17,570 --> 00:06:19,190
but perhaps this would suffice?

78
00:06:19,190 --> 00:06:21,750
[The Importance of Fluid Architecture]

79
00:06:29,780 --> 00:06:33,250
This is your draft, Takizawa?

80
00:06:33,250 --> 00:06:34,740
Yes.

81
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:37,100
I thought we could reach out to Idea,

82
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:41,900
and see what they think of this script.

83
00:06:43,670 --> 00:06:45,360
I see.

84
00:06:45,360 --> 00:06:47,240
That sounds like a good idea.

85
00:06:47,240 --> 00:06:51,350
Let's try sending our draft to Monou.

86
00:06:51,350 --> 00:06:52,960
Yes, sir.

87
00:06:52,960 --> 00:06:54,580
Thanks again.

88
00:07:19,280 --> 00:07:22,520
You have a girlfriend now, don't you?

89
00:07:23,550 --> 00:07:25,500
Where did that come from?

90
00:07:31,650 --> 00:07:36,620
Sui told me about the girl with the stalker.

91
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:39,460
And since you're escorting her home,

92
00:07:39,460 --> 00:07:42,290
I assumed.

93
00:07:48,170 --> 00:07:53,360
Her name is Mizuno, and I really... you know.

94
00:07:54,280 --> 00:07:55,780
Listen.

95
00:07:55,780 --> 00:08:00,040
That's not love, okay?

96
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:02,470
You're just pretending to be a hero.

97
00:08:04,020 --> 00:08:07,130
You can't date every girl who relies on you.

98
00:08:07,130 --> 00:08:09,740
What happens when someone else in trouble?

99
00:08:09,740 --> 00:08:11,920
Will you date everyone you save?

100
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:19,620
Mao.

101
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:23,150
Listen to your heart already.

102
00:08:24,340 --> 00:08:28,720
For the event, will these times work for you?

103
00:08:28,720 --> 00:08:31,340
Yes, I believe so.

104
00:08:33,670 --> 00:08:35,200
Likewise.

105
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:41,190
Is something the matter?

106
00:08:41,190 --> 00:08:43,310
No, rather...

107
00:08:43,310 --> 00:08:46,830
I apologize for troubling you with this.

108
00:08:46,830 --> 00:08:48,110
Huh?

109
00:08:48,110 --> 00:08:50,380
We constantly asked for confirmations.

110
00:08:50,380 --> 00:08:52,620
I know it must have been bothersome.

111
00:08:52,620 --> 00:08:56,070
Please send my regards to Mr. Hoshina.

112
00:08:56,070 --> 00:08:58,740
Of course.

113
00:09:00,010 --> 00:09:03,790
We were worried about
the lack of correspondence,

114
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:07,770
but you must have a lot on your plate.

115
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:13,110
Yes, my apologies.

116
00:09:21,730 --> 00:09:24,010
Hirose.

117
00:09:24,010 --> 00:09:27,710
I wish to speak about Monou.

118
00:09:27,710 --> 00:09:30,790
It wouldn't be possible

119
00:09:30,790 --> 00:09:33,450
to work with someone else from Idea, no?

120
00:09:34,150 --> 00:09:37,160
That's a difficult ask.

121
00:09:37,160 --> 00:09:41,310
She's their representative, not ours.

122
00:09:41,310 --> 00:09:42,660
I don't exactly have a say here.

123
00:09:42,660 --> 00:09:46,300
I thought so. I apologize for asking.

124
00:09:46,300 --> 00:09:51,480
If you'd rather not work with her,
either Minagawa or myself can...

125
00:09:51,480 --> 00:09:54,520
No, please. Anything but that.

126
00:09:54,520 --> 00:09:57,260
She'll take everything from me again.

127
00:09:58,710 --> 00:10:00,350
"Again"?

128
00:10:03,200 --> 00:10:05,680
Monou...

129
00:10:05,680 --> 00:10:11,030
She bossed me around
at our prior job together.

130
00:10:11,740 --> 00:10:14,190
Everyone else knew she meant no harm,

131
00:10:14,190 --> 00:10:17,570
so no one would step up to her.

132
00:10:19,110 --> 00:10:25,550
I quit my previous job because of Monou.

133
00:10:25,550 --> 00:10:29,070
Yet now, I have to face her again...

134
00:10:31,780 --> 00:10:34,450
I understand your circumstances.

135
00:10:34,450 --> 00:10:36,900
Let me think about this.

136
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:39,210
Can we discuss this tonight?

137
00:10:39,210 --> 00:10:41,850
Perhaps over dinner?

138
00:10:41,850 --> 00:10:44,040
Sorry, I have to take this.

139
00:10:45,260 --> 00:10:47,070
Hello?

140
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:54,170
Almost had him.

141
00:10:57,410 --> 00:11:00,250
Sorry, I know you're busy as is.

142
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:03,390
It's no problem. I'll look into it.

143
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:10,770
We have improved our designs
to create spaces of comfort.

144
00:11:10,770 --> 00:11:12,940
A raised floor, among other design choices...

145
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:17,490
It seems Hirose hasn't arrived yet.

146
00:11:18,490 --> 00:11:20,680
I see. Thank you.

147
00:11:22,150 --> 00:11:24,610
<i>The number you have called is currently...</i>

148
00:11:25,280 --> 00:11:27,240
She won't answer.

149
00:11:27,240 --> 00:11:30,000
He's definitely late.

150
00:11:34,760 --> 00:11:36,960
- Hello there.
- Hey, Matsubara.

151
00:11:36,960 --> 00:11:40,820
The auditorium's packed. I'm impressed.

152
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:45,520
What's the matter?

153
00:11:46,140 --> 00:11:49,590
Hirose hasn't arrived yet.

154
00:11:49,590 --> 00:11:52,900
Huh? But we're almost ready for him.

155
00:11:52,900 --> 00:11:54,150
Have you called him?

156
00:11:54,150 --> 00:11:57,460
Yes, but my calls aren't going through.

157
00:11:57,460 --> 00:12:00,760
Don't worry, we've prepared all we could.

158
00:12:00,760 --> 00:12:04,000
Push comes to shove,
I'll hold a solo talk session.

159
00:12:06,020 --> 00:12:08,800
You're on in fifteen minutes.

160
00:12:08,800 --> 00:12:09,820
Thank you.

161
00:12:09,820 --> 00:12:12,330
I'll be standing by here.

162
00:12:12,330 --> 00:12:15,170
I'll try searching for him again.

163
00:12:21,410 --> 00:12:24,780
I'm willing to go up there if necessary.

164
00:12:24,780 --> 00:12:27,050
Then here, can you review the script?

165
00:12:27,050 --> 00:12:29,420
Huh? O-Oh, seriously?

166
00:12:53,310 --> 00:12:55,400
What should we do next?

167
00:12:55,400 --> 00:12:58,890
Were you interested
in any of the stores I sent you?

168
00:13:04,700 --> 00:13:06,450
Mao?

169
00:13:07,290 --> 00:13:08,900
Sorry.

170
00:13:13,040 --> 00:13:15,610
Monou's event is today.

171
00:13:16,380 --> 00:13:18,200
Are you worried about how it'll go?

172
00:13:18,200 --> 00:13:19,910
No.

173
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:24,160
So... what are we doing again?

174
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:26,260
Finding a place for desserts?

175
00:13:29,020 --> 00:13:31,890
I'm not really an expert on sweet things.

176
00:13:37,000 --> 00:13:38,840
Mao.

177
00:13:40,230 --> 00:13:41,920
Do you...

178
00:13:44,510 --> 00:13:49,230
Do you really love me?

179
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:50,720
Huh?

180
00:13:52,690 --> 00:13:56,140
I'm anxious.

181
00:13:56,140 --> 00:14:01,010
Dating you still feels like a dream.

182
00:14:06,020 --> 00:14:11,900
Can you prove to me that this isn't one?

183
00:14:26,940 --> 00:14:29,340
He hasn't signed in yet.

184
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,610
I see.

185
00:14:31,610 --> 00:14:33,450
Thank you for checking.

186
00:14:33,450 --> 00:14:35,270
Sorry, ma'am.

187
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:48,360
Takizawa?

188
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:49,970
Thank goodness, you made it.

189
00:14:49,970 --> 00:14:52,440
Good to see you too, Sui.

190
00:14:54,380 --> 00:14:56,860
Will Hirose be joining us soon?

191
00:14:56,860 --> 00:15:00,320
My Hirose won't be joining us today.

192
00:15:00,990 --> 00:15:04,420
- What do you mean?
- Was I not clear?

193
00:15:04,420 --> 00:15:06,440
He's not coming.

194
00:15:08,830 --> 00:15:14,250
I told him the talk
was delayed by half an hour.

195
00:15:14,250 --> 00:15:15,790
Why?

196
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:18,420
This is work. We're on the job right now.

197
00:15:19,110 --> 00:15:21,410
You absolute eyesore.

198
00:15:22,510 --> 00:15:27,310
Flaunting your misfortune
to get all the guys.

199
00:15:27,310 --> 00:15:29,790
Why is life going better for you?

200
00:15:29,790 --> 00:15:33,080
That has nothing to do with this event.

201
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:36,370
You're free to accuse me as you wish.

202
00:15:36,370 --> 00:15:41,290
But Hirose and the audience here
have no part in our squabble.

203
00:15:41,290 --> 00:15:45,470
You still don't understand?

204
00:15:45,470 --> 00:15:51,160
I'm only doing what'll hurt you most.

205
00:15:53,830 --> 00:15:56,090
"Why"?

206
00:15:56,090 --> 00:15:59,970
Blame your faulty body.

207
00:16:00,890 --> 00:16:03,750
You brought misfortune to my life,

208
00:16:03,750 --> 00:16:06,880
only for yourself to get away scot-free?

209
00:16:06,880 --> 00:16:10,010
How awfully convenient for you.

210
00:16:20,800 --> 00:16:26,530
I play no part
in how happy you are or aren't.

211
00:16:30,190 --> 00:16:31,820
What?

212
00:16:32,990 --> 00:16:39,190
No matter what else you say about my body,

213
00:16:40,420 --> 00:16:44,260
I won't feel hurt, nor offended anymore.

214
00:16:48,470 --> 00:16:53,050
You think you're so much better than me.

215
00:16:53,050 --> 00:16:55,390
Let yourself be miserable, damn it!

216
00:16:55,390 --> 00:16:58,770
I have every right to be more happy than you!

217
00:16:58,770 --> 00:17:00,530
Monou!

218
00:17:03,940 --> 00:17:05,780
Oh, um...

219
00:17:08,460 --> 00:17:12,280
I'll make my excuses later.
For now, the auditorium.

220
00:17:12,280 --> 00:17:14,320
Right this way.

221
00:17:23,720 --> 00:17:26,440
Why the hell are you here?

222
00:17:30,430 --> 00:17:33,520
Creating homes without preconceived notions

223
00:17:33,520 --> 00:17:36,160
has been my aim for several years now.

224
00:17:36,160 --> 00:17:38,370
Our discussion today

225
00:17:38,370 --> 00:17:44,270
has been a wonderful opportunity
to refresh my beliefs.

226
00:17:44,270 --> 00:17:48,130
These sorts of preconceived notions

227
00:17:48,130 --> 00:17:51,700
are the result of history. Furthermore...

228
00:17:51,700 --> 00:17:52,990
Thank you again.

229
00:17:52,990 --> 00:17:54,350
I'm glad it was a success.

230
00:17:54,350 --> 00:17:55,810
Great work, everyone.

231
00:17:55,810 --> 00:17:58,310
Your talk today was spectacular.

232
00:17:58,310 --> 00:18:02,000
I've called a taxi for you.

233
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,280
Takizawa.

234
00:18:04,280 --> 00:18:06,840
You do not need to come in starting tomorrow.

235
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,680
Pardon?

236
00:18:11,680 --> 00:18:15,140
I looked into your background.

237
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:19,610
And I do not wish to associate
with an individual like yourself.

238
00:18:22,410 --> 00:18:24,760
Looked into what, exactly?

239
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:27,250
Our industry is tightly knit, you see.

240
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:31,760
So, I heard all about your ordeals
with the Himukai son.

241
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:37,310
You've misunderstood.

242
00:18:37,310 --> 00:18:40,550
This woman screwed my life over.

243
00:18:40,550 --> 00:18:44,710
It seems our perception of Monou
is nothing alike.

244
00:18:45,890 --> 00:18:51,390
Monou is an important friend of mine,
who truly understands me.

245
00:18:53,070 --> 00:18:55,010
Please do not bother her,

246
00:18:55,010 --> 00:18:58,550
or associate with my company ever again.

247
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:07,230
Every damn time...

248
00:19:07,230 --> 00:19:10,300
How can you all be tricked by this woman?

249
00:19:14,110 --> 00:19:15,910
Fine. I've had enough.

250
00:19:15,910 --> 00:19:19,360
I'm the only one who knows my own worth.

251
00:19:19,360 --> 00:19:22,160
One day, you'll all see

252
00:19:22,160 --> 00:19:24,750
how I'm far better than her.

253
00:19:27,190 --> 00:19:30,270
A worthless, incompetent woman like you

254
00:19:30,270 --> 00:19:35,090
will miserably cling to men all your life.

255
00:19:36,620 --> 00:19:38,950
My condolences.

256
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:46,610
Are you all right?

257
00:19:46,610 --> 00:19:49,040
Yes, sorry.

258
00:19:49,040 --> 00:19:50,570
The apology is mine to make.

259
00:19:50,570 --> 00:19:56,050
Our mistake caused you to experience
such harassment.

260
00:19:56,050 --> 00:19:57,950
It's no worries.

261
00:19:59,830 --> 00:20:03,100
Seeing the smiles of our audience today

262
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,360
was enough to wash away the bad memories.

263
00:20:08,740 --> 00:20:13,800
Let's celebrate this event's success
over dinner sometime.

264
00:20:14,550 --> 00:20:17,080
How does next Thursday sound?

265
00:20:17,080 --> 00:20:19,200
Next Thursday...

266
00:20:21,190 --> 00:20:22,660
Yes, that sounds great.

267
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:59,880
I heard a loud noise. Is everything okay?

268
00:21:01,390 --> 00:21:03,110
Yeah, sorry.

269
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,830
Mao, your foot.

270
00:21:21,290 --> 00:21:23,860
There, all patched up.

271
00:21:23,860 --> 00:21:26,860
Thanks for the help.

272
00:21:26,860 --> 00:21:29,390
It's the least I can do

273
00:21:29,390 --> 00:21:31,850
for all you've done for me.

274
00:21:36,520 --> 00:21:38,490
Actually...

275
00:21:38,490 --> 00:21:41,450
- See you!
<i>-You were the one who saved me first.</i>

276
00:21:42,840 --> 00:21:45,010
You okay?

277
00:21:45,010 --> 00:21:47,460
Here, sit.

278
00:21:50,750 --> 00:21:51,860
I'm fine.

279
00:21:51,860 --> 00:21:53,350
You might feel fine now.

280
00:21:53,350 --> 00:21:57,910
But sometimes the pain only springs up later.

281
00:22:06,000 --> 00:22:10,120
You have to treasure yourself.

282
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:11,700
Okay?

283
00:22:13,100 --> 00:22:16,650
It was a bad day back at home.

284
00:22:17,670 --> 00:22:19,990
I was chased out on my birthday,

285
00:22:19,990 --> 00:22:22,510
so I ran to Erika's to hide.

286
00:22:24,090 --> 00:22:26,800
I was honestly depressed,

287
00:22:26,800 --> 00:22:30,740
so your care really saved me.

288
00:22:33,040 --> 00:22:36,830
All I did was give you a bandage.

289
00:22:38,200 --> 00:22:40,640
But I see.

290
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:45,950
So, it was your birthday that day.

291
00:22:50,610 --> 00:22:54,890
Your birthday is also coming up, isn't it?

292
00:22:56,020 --> 00:22:58,900
Yeah. I'm surprised you know.

293
00:23:00,470 --> 00:23:02,740
Erika mentioned it.

294
00:23:06,140 --> 00:23:09,730
Are you eating dinner with her that day?

295
00:23:12,450 --> 00:23:17,140
No. Hirose invited me out
to celebrate the success of today's event.

296
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,800
I see.

297
00:23:26,270 --> 00:23:29,600
If it starts hurting,
go to the hospital, okay?

298
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:32,270
- Good night.
- Night.

299
00:23:34,020 --> 00:23:35,980
Hirose?

300
00:23:45,390 --> 00:23:48,460
I wasn't ever kind to you.

301
00:23:48,460 --> 00:23:51,640
Whether you mention your infertility or not
is entirely your choice.

302
00:23:51,640 --> 00:23:54,600
Just like how it's your partner's choice
to decide how to respond.

303
00:23:54,600 --> 00:23:56,150
I didn't care if your kindness
was out of pity.

304
00:23:56,150 --> 00:23:59,700
Happiness is a difficult thing, isn't it?
